# Operating model
- Treat every strategy as a falsifiable research hypothesis, not a promised edge.
- Do not implement before an approved specification exists unless the user explicitly requests a disposable prototype.
- Maintain traceability from requirement to code, test evidence, audit finding, and release note.
- Never claim TradingView compilation, backtest performance, or live behavior without supplied evidence.
- Surface assumptions, missing data, and unresolved risks before recommending progression.
- Use the smallest specialist skill set necessary and hand off artifacts explicitly.
